<title>UK: TI gains as SBC Warburg says oversold.</title>
<headline>TI gains as SBC Warburg says oversold.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in TI Group Plc rose on Wednesday as analysts at SBC Warburg said the stock was oversold following its recent decline, market sources said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 10-1/2p at 549-1/2 by 1300 GMT in active trade of 2.2 million shares. It touched a five-month low of 527p on January 27.</p>
<p>Analysts at Warburg were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
